WEBVTT

00:16.433 --> 00:18.162
What you doing?

00:18.568 --> 00:21.765
Building an original 1978 Firebird.

00:21.938 --> 00:22.962
I got it on eBay.

00:23.473 --> 00:25.441
Okay. Why?

00:25.875 --> 00:27.934
I had this model when I was little,
remember?

00:28.111 --> 00:31.911
Spent a month building it and painting it
and putting on all the decals.

00:32.082 --> 00:34.710
Is that the one I tried
to make a bong out of?

00:34.918 --> 00:37.045
No, that was my Munster Mobile...

00:38.188 --> 00:40.156
...and my ventriloquist dummy...

00:40.323 --> 00:43.520
...and my Rock 'em Sock 'em Robots.

00:43.927 --> 00:47.829
My Firebird you blowtorched with
a cigarette lighter and Mom's Aqua Net.

00:47.997 --> 00:51.057
Oh, yeah, the Firebird.

00:51.234 --> 00:55.034
Anyway, I loved that model,
and now I'm gonna have it again.

00:55.205 --> 00:57.070
I am gonna have it again, right?

00:57.574 --> 00:59.769
Relax. If I destroy any of your cars...

00:59.943 --> 01:03.071
...it'll be that oil-dripping piece of crap
out there in my garage.

01:17.293 --> 01:19.284
I'm worried about my brother.

01:20.697 --> 01:21.857
Why?

01:22.031 --> 01:26.365
Well, he's either so lonely
he's trying to recapture his childhood...

01:26.536 --> 01:29.096
...which was not that good
in the first place...

01:29.572 --> 01:32.473
...or he's created an elaborate ruse
to hide the fact...

01:32.642 --> 01:35.372
...that he's become
a degenerate glue-sniffer.

01:36.012 --> 01:37.912
To be honest, I'm rooting for the glue.

01:38.982 --> 01:43.180
- I've been meaning to talk to you about him.
- You want him gone? He's gone. I love you.

01:43.353 --> 01:45.753
No, no, he's a wonderful guy.

01:45.922 --> 01:48.413
I have a friend
I think might be a good match for him.

01:48.591 --> 01:50.786
Oh, no, you're wrong.

01:51.594 --> 01:53.562
Come on, Charlie.

01:53.930 --> 01:55.420
Listen.

02:03.406 --> 02:06.034
You don't wanna do that to a friend,
do you?

02:06.209 --> 02:09.110
Alan's a doll.
He just needs to find the right woman.

02:09.479 --> 02:13.074
If you check his closet,
you'll find the right woman is a doll.

02:14.117 --> 02:18.076
At least let me try. I'll set up a dinner
with the four of us. It'll be fun.

02:18.254 --> 02:19.346
For who?

02:19.522 --> 02:22.923
It's bad enough you wanna punish
your friend. Why do I have to suffer?

02:23.459 --> 02:26.656
Isn't it worth one night of your life
to maybe make two people happy?

02:26.830 --> 02:31.233
That's not fair. I always come off bad
when I answer questions like that truthfully.

02:32.235 --> 02:33.600
Just do it for me.

02:35.338 --> 02:37.135
Is that a yes?

02:39.442 --> 02:41.740
Remember those words
when we go to bed tonight.

02:41.911 --> 02:44.641
- What words?
- "Just do it for me."

02:47.417 --> 02:48.441
So anyway...

02:48.618 --> 02:52.748
...he's Charlie's brother and a very
sweet guy, and I really think you'll like him.

02:56.059 --> 02:57.754
Boy, I don't know.

02:57.927 --> 02:59.189
Blind dates.

02:59.362 --> 03:02.627
You never know what kind of freak
you're gonna end up with.

03:12.508 --> 03:14.635
- So you don't know her name?
- Nope.

03:14.811 --> 03:17.041
- And you don't know what she does?
- Nope.

03:17.213 --> 03:19.909
- And you don't know what she looks like?
- What do you care?

03:20.083 --> 03:24.179
&lt;i>You were gonna spend the night building
a scale model of The Dukes of Hazzard car.&lt;/i>

03:25.188 --> 03:27.656
Uh, actually,
I just finished the General Lee.

03:27.824 --> 03:31.282
&lt;i>Now I'm working on Burt Reynolds'
Trans Am from Smokey and the Bandit.&lt;/i>

03:32.295 --> 03:35.822
Okay, okay. Just promise me
you won't bring any of that up tonight.

03:35.999 --> 03:37.660
- Why?
- Why?

03:40.136 --> 03:42.001
You're asking me
why a 40-year-old man...

03:42.171 --> 03:45.368
...shouldn't talk about model cars
on a first date?

03:45.541 --> 03:48.738
Hmm. I see your point.
Leave a little mystery.

03:49.412 --> 03:52.313
Yeah, that's my point.

03:52.482 --> 03:53.506
Come on.

03:53.683 --> 03:56.311
Oh, speaking of mystery,
I am currently the high bidder...

03:56.486 --> 04:00.047
...on an original mint in the box
Scooby-Doo Mystery Machine.

04:05.061 --> 04:06.119
How do I look?

04:06.296 --> 04:09.527
Don't open that can of worms.
You are what you are.

04:11.668 --> 04:13.158
There's Chelsea.

04:15.738 --> 04:18.866
- Sorry, we're late.
No, no, we were early.

04:25.815 --> 04:27.783
Charlie, Alan, this is my friend, Rose.

04:27.951 --> 04:30.419
Rose, this is Charlie and Alan.

04:30.920 --> 04:32.217
It's nice to meet you, Alan.

04:33.022 --> 04:34.353
No, that's Charlie.

04:34.791 --> 04:38.124
Ooh. Even better. Hi, Alan.

04:39.329 --> 04:40.819
Hi.

04:41.864 --> 04:43.695
Why don't we all sit down?

04:43.866 --> 04:46.391
So many reasons.

04:48.571 --> 04:50.664
Chelsea's told me so much about you,
boys.

04:50.840 --> 04:52.808
It's so nice to finally meet you.

04:53.910 --> 04:56.276
Alan, I understand you're a chiropractor.

04:59.282 --> 05:00.840
Yes.

05:01.050 --> 05:03.143
I am a chiropractor.

05:03.820 --> 05:05.253
Charlie?

05:05.822 --> 05:07.346
Yes...

05:07.523 --> 05:09.650
...he is a chiropractor.

05:10.593 --> 05:12.754
Oh, that's just terrific.

05:12.929 --> 05:14.590
And what do you do, Charlie?

05:15.031 --> 05:16.259
Um...

05:16.432 --> 05:20.061
I write kids songs and jingles.

05:21.004 --> 05:22.403
Alan?

05:23.673 --> 05:27.769
Yes, he writes kids songs and jingles.

05:30.913 --> 05:32.437
And I am a chiropractor.

05:35.885 --> 05:37.375
Yes...

05:37.687 --> 05:38.779
...he's a chiropractor.

05:40.857 --> 05:42.484
They don't get out much, do they?

05:43.259 --> 05:44.385
Apparently not.

05:44.560 --> 05:46.960
So, Chels...

05:47.130 --> 05:50.156
- ...where did you meet...?
- Rose.

05:50.700 --> 05:51.826
Right.

05:54.704 --> 05:56.365
Rose.

05:56.973 --> 05:58.702
- Yoga class.
- No kidding.

05:58.875 --> 06:02.140
Yeah. And then we ran into each other
at Pilates...

06:02.812 --> 06:06.441
...and the manicurist and jogging
and the dry cleaner.

06:07.183 --> 06:09.947
- Crazy, huh?
- Sure are. Sure is.

06:11.988 --> 06:15.048
Seemed like every time I turned around,
there she was.

06:15.224 --> 06:18.216
Seemed like every time I turned around,
there you were.

06:18.394 --> 06:20.191
I thought maybe you were stalking me.

06:26.803 --> 06:28.464
- That's funny.
- Good one. Yeah.

06:30.873 --> 06:32.864
Can I start you off with cocktails?

06:33.042 --> 06:35.237
I think I need to stay sober tonight.

06:36.679 --> 06:40.012
- But you guys go ahead.
- I'll have a chardonnay. I'll be right back.

06:41.417 --> 06:44.511
I'll go with you.
I'll have a double vodka rocks.

06:46.422 --> 06:48.219
I feel a little reckless tonight.

06:49.892 --> 06:51.416
Fun personality, huh?

06:51.861 --> 06:53.328
Yeah.

06:53.930 --> 06:57.229
Unfortunately,
she's got six more of them.

06:58.101 --> 07:00.399
- And for you, sir?
- Whiskey, neat.

07:00.870 --> 07:03.634
- Since when do you drink hard liquor?
- Since right now.

07:03.806 --> 07:06.070
I'd order a glass of crack
if it were on the menu.

07:07.543 --> 07:09.306
True that.

07:11.214 --> 07:13.682
- Why didn't you say something?
- Why didn't you?

07:13.850 --> 07:15.681
- I was following your lead.
- What lead?

07:15.852 --> 07:18.320
The minute I saw her,
I practically peed my pants.

07:18.488 --> 07:20.115
Well then, I did follow your lead.

07:20.289 --> 07:21.756
So, what are we gonna do now?

07:22.258 --> 07:24.249
I don't know. I guess we play along.

07:24.427 --> 07:26.452
Play along? Are you serious?

07:26.629 --> 07:28.859
What am I supposed to do, Alan?
Tell the truth?

07:29.031 --> 07:30.396
Oh, Chelsea, I almost forgot.

07:30.566 --> 07:33.626
Your new BFF and I had a one-night stand,
and when I dumped her...

07:33.803 --> 07:36.897
...she superglued my nut sack to my thigh
and started stalking me.

07:37.907 --> 07:41.001
I thought maybe I was in love with her
and followed her to England.

07:41.177 --> 07:42.337
And when she came back...

07:42.512 --> 07:45.310
...I thought I was dying
and almost asked her to marry me.

07:46.282 --> 07:49.080
Yeah, when you put it in story form
it really does sound bad.

07:49.952 --> 07:53.615
So we play along until I can find out
what Rose's angle is.

07:54.023 --> 07:56.856
- So I'm supposed to date her?
- Stop flattering yourself.

07:57.026 --> 07:59.290
This isn't about you.
It's me she's interested in.

07:59.462 --> 08:01.760
What are you saying,
I'm not good enough for her?

08:01.931 --> 08:04.126
You want that loony-toon
as a girlfriend?

08:04.300 --> 08:07.133
No. But I am currently unattached.

08:10.106 --> 08:11.334
Now, you listen to me.

08:11.507 --> 08:14.840
This is a blind date that goes no further,
you understand?

08:15.011 --> 08:16.342
I got it.

08:21.117 --> 08:22.812
She really likes him.

08:22.985 --> 08:24.179
Swell.

08:40.937 --> 08:43.269
I thought there was
real chemistry between them.

08:43.973 --> 08:46.032
I'm sure they have some meds
in common.

08:48.844 --> 08:51.438
- But I wouldn't get your hopes up.
- Why not?

08:52.515 --> 08:53.777
She's not his type.

08:53.950 --> 08:57.442
What do you mean?
She's pretty, smart, rich.

08:57.620 --> 09:00.851
Okay, then he's not her type.

09:06.696 --> 09:09.893
- This is crazy.
- I know.

09:10.399 --> 09:12.333
We just met.

09:33.456 --> 09:38.393
Oh, no, no, no, you idiot.

09:39.962 --> 09:42.396
- Morning, Charlie
- Morning.

09:44.867 --> 09:48.325
Should've smothered him in the crib
when I had the chance.

09:50.773 --> 09:53.105
Boy, take one day off
for a poker tournament...

09:53.276 --> 09:55.107
...and you miss a whole lot
around here.

09:57.880 --> 10:01.338
- You said you were sick.
- I was healed. It's a miracle.

10:02.785 --> 10:03.809
You wanna catch me up?

10:04.220 --> 10:07.986
Chelsea set Alan up on a blind date
with a girl she met at yoga class.

10:08.424 --> 10:11.689
- What's he doing with Rose?
- She's the girl.

10:12.161 --> 10:13.492
Oh.

10:13.829 --> 10:16.320
Diabolical, heh.

10:17.900 --> 10:19.094
So Chelsea doesn't know?

10:19.268 --> 10:21.759
Chelsea knows nothing,
and I wanna keep it that way.

10:21.937 --> 10:23.336
Okay.

10:23.506 --> 10:24.996
Why is Alan playing along?

10:25.174 --> 10:27.005
Because Alan is a horny idiot.

10:28.611 --> 10:32.377
And horny idiots are perfectly willing
to have sex with crazy girls.

10:33.683 --> 10:35.310
Yeah, I know, but I've grown.

10:37.887 --> 10:39.013
Charlie, did you see?

10:39.789 --> 10:41.188
Yeah, I saw.

10:41.791 --> 10:43.986
Told you they'd hit it off.
Didn't I tell you?

10:44.527 --> 10:45.551
You told me.

10:46.429 --> 10:48.659
I'm a little worried
they're moving so fast.

10:48.831 --> 10:51.629
Yeah, that's the worrisome part.

10:52.802 --> 10:54.861
Berta, have you met Rose yet?

11:05.181 --> 11:07.581
Screw it, I'm going home.

11:09.985 --> 11:11.145
Feel better.

11:18.027 --> 11:19.995
Cut it out. Cut it out.

11:20.162 --> 11:22.722
Stop it. Stop it.

11:28.104 --> 11:29.594
Hello.

11:29.805 --> 11:31.067
Sit down.

11:31.607 --> 11:33.370
Um... You know I have company.

11:33.542 --> 11:35.772
Yes, I know you have company,
now sit down.

11:38.748 --> 11:40.238
Okay.

11:49.592 --> 11:50.991
What's up?

11:54.563 --> 11:55.996
Explain it to me, Alan.

11:56.165 --> 11:57.632
Help me understand.

11:58.534 --> 11:59.558
You mean, Rose?

11:59.735 --> 12:03.068
No, I mean the internal combustion engine.
Yes, Rose.

12:05.541 --> 12:08.942
Uh, well, we started talking
on the ride home last night...

12:09.111 --> 12:11.102
...and we really hit it off.

12:11.280 --> 12:12.747
She has changed, Charlie.

12:13.416 --> 12:15.111
Changed?

12:15.284 --> 12:16.717
She was stalking my fiancée.

12:16.886 --> 12:19.252
Ah, ah.
Well, actually, she explained all that.

12:19.422 --> 12:21.117
Really? What did she say?

12:21.357 --> 12:23.052
Uh, well...

12:23.793 --> 12:27.524
I don't remember all the details because
she was tweaking my nipples at the time.

12:29.698 --> 12:32.394
Oh. Hi, Charlie.

12:32.568 --> 12:36.129
- All right, Rose, what are you up to?
- What do you mean?

12:36.872 --> 12:38.840
I'm telling you right now.

12:39.008 --> 12:42.671
I love Chelsea, and if you mess things up
with us, I will never forgive you.

12:43.145 --> 12:44.476
Wow.

12:44.647 --> 12:46.740
What did I ever do to deserve that?

12:49.285 --> 12:51.583
- You're kidding, right?
- Yeah.

12:55.758 --> 12:59.489
So once again, what are you up to?

13:00.095 --> 13:04.054
Okay, at first I was just doing
a little light recon on Chelsea...

13:04.233 --> 13:06.428
...to make sure
you weren't dating a wackjob.

13:07.536 --> 13:10.266
You thought Chelsea might be-

13:10.573 --> 13:12.006
Go on.

13:12.174 --> 13:14.005
Well, good news, she's not.

13:14.176 --> 13:16.371
She's got a cousin
who's a truck-stop hooker...

13:16.545 --> 13:19.139
...and her mom's an honorary Kleagle
in the Ku Klux Klan.

13:19.315 --> 13:21.545
But Chelsea is clean as a whistle.

13:22.418 --> 13:24.682
- Kleagle?
- According to Wikipedia...

13:24.854 --> 13:28.915
...it's below Grand Dragon
and above Exalted Cyclops.

13:29.525 --> 13:30.753
Whatever.

13:30.926 --> 13:33.827
But what's the deal
with the lunch lady here?

13:39.068 --> 13:40.160
Alan?

13:40.336 --> 13:43.066
Well, that was Chelsea's idea, not mine.

13:43.239 --> 13:44.638
I tried to get out of it.

13:44.807 --> 13:46.968
- Really?
- I'm sorry, sweetie...

13:47.142 --> 13:51.511
...but I thought a double date with Charlie
and his fiancée might be a little awkward.

13:51.914 --> 13:55.315
A little awkward?
When I saw you sitting there...

13:55.484 --> 13:59.147
...my sphincter slammed shut so quickly
you could've used it as a cigar cutter.

14:02.191 --> 14:04.523
Yeah, you should've seen your face.

14:05.928 --> 14:07.156
Anyway...

14:07.329 --> 14:09.763
...it all worked out for the best.

14:09.932 --> 14:13.333
Last night, I saw a side of your brother
that I've never seen before.

14:13.769 --> 14:15.134
What side?

14:15.304 --> 14:16.601
He's only got the two.

14:16.772 --> 14:19.605
"Oh, no, here he comes"
and "Oh, good, he's leaving."

14:20.643 --> 14:23.476
Look, Charlie. this has nothing to do
with you and Chelsea.

14:23.646 --> 14:26.240
This has nothing to do with you and Rose.
The fact is...

14:26.415 --> 14:30.249
...we really like each other,
and we wanna keep seeing each other.

14:30.452 --> 14:33.216
And we'd really like your blessing.

14:34.456 --> 14:36.583
So you actually wanna be with him?

14:36.759 --> 14:38.021
I do.

14:38.193 --> 14:41.424
And you believe she's got
no ulterior motive whatsoever?

14:42.031 --> 14:43.521
I do.

14:45.334 --> 14:46.426
Fine.

14:46.602 --> 14:48.729
I now pronounce you
fruit basket and nutcase.

14:52.174 --> 14:54.608
May God have mercy on your souls.

14:55.644 --> 14:56.941
Yay.

14:57.112 --> 14:59.080
I don't think that was really a blessing.

14:59.682 --> 15:02.412
It doesn't matter.
So, what are we doing this afternoon?

15:02.585 --> 15:06.214
Oh, gee, I gotta pick up Jake.
I promised him I'd take him to the movies.

15:06.388 --> 15:08.982
- You know, a little father-son time.
- Oh, that's sweet.

15:09.425 --> 15:12.019
Well, just call me
when you wanna get together again.

15:12.194 --> 15:15.322
- Sure. Or you can call me.
- Okay.

15:32.881 --> 15:36.044
Hello? Oh, Jake, thank God.

15:37.853 --> 15:41.880
Uh, nothing.
Oh, wait, hang on, I got another call.

15:42.057 --> 15:43.388
Hello?

15:45.260 --> 15:47.990
Yes, Rose, this is my number.

15:51.066 --> 15:55.503
- So how'd you like the movie?
- It was an insult to my intelligence.

15:56.672 --> 15:58.037
Really?

15:58.207 --> 16:00.835
Everybody knows zombies
can't ride motorcycles.

16:01.276 --> 16:02.709
Yeah, that bumped me too.

16:03.145 --> 16:06.114
And why would they wear helmets?
They're dead.

16:06.281 --> 16:07.646
Another good point.

16:07.816 --> 16:10.944
I don't know who they're making movies
for these days.

16:11.120 --> 16:13.588
Fine, next time you pick.

16:14.590 --> 16:17.115
Anyway, there's something
I wanna talk to you about.

16:17.292 --> 16:21.854
Oh, come on, it was one fart during
the previews, and everybody laughed.

16:22.498 --> 16:24.363
No, no, not that.

16:24.533 --> 16:27.058
I just want you to know
that I've been dating somebody.

16:27.236 --> 16:28.635
You might be meeting her soon.

16:29.004 --> 16:30.494
Oh, okay, good.

16:30.673 --> 16:34.734
- So you have no problem with that?
- Not at all. You should have a girlfriend.

16:34.910 --> 16:36.036
You think so?

16:36.211 --> 16:38.736
Yeah. The model car stuff
was starting to freak me out.

16:41.083 --> 16:44.246
I mean, seriously, you're a grown man.

16:46.388 --> 16:48.083
What the hell?

16:48.257 --> 16:50.987
You didn't call me!

16:52.428 --> 16:55.261
- Hi, Rose.
- Hey, Jake.

16:59.935 --> 17:02.096
So tell me about your new girlfriend.

17:08.811 --> 17:12.076
I'm so glad you forgave me
for my little outburst in the car.

17:12.247 --> 17:15.546
Well, you have a very compelling way
of apologizing.

17:17.319 --> 17:19.685
But we need to have a little talk
about boundaries.

17:20.422 --> 17:23.152
It was just my pinky, Alan.

17:26.795 --> 17:28.592
No, no, that was fun.

17:30.532 --> 17:33.433
Is it about me following you and Jake
into the movie theater?

17:33.602 --> 17:35.433
You followed us into the movie theater?

17:36.505 --> 17:38.700
No.

17:40.242 --> 17:42.972
Look, Rose, I really like you.

17:43.145 --> 17:47.411
But you've got to realize that people need
their space and you need to respect that.

17:48.751 --> 17:50.082
All right.

17:51.053 --> 17:52.645
So we're clear on that?

17:53.088 --> 17:54.953
Yes, I'm sorry.

17:55.124 --> 17:56.318
It won't happen again.

17:58.293 --> 17:59.658
Good.

18:01.263 --> 18:04.027
- Well, good night.
- Good night.

18:10.739 --> 18:14.140
Boy, this is an Alan Harper
I haven't seen before.

18:14.309 --> 18:15.606
Uh-huh.

18:15.778 --> 18:18.770
Forceful, confident.

18:18.947 --> 18:20.437
Thank you.

18:21.517 --> 18:23.985
I don't like him very much.

18:34.630 --> 18:36.461
Morning, Charlie.

18:38.233 --> 18:40.064
- Morning, Rose.
- Alan needs his space.

18:40.235 --> 18:42.203
- I'm gonna give it to him.
- Okay.

18:42.371 --> 18:45.306
- Say hi to Chelsea for me.
- Will do.

18:50.913 --> 18:52.380
Oh, I got a bad feeling.

18:59.121 --> 19:00.452
Alan?

19:00.622 --> 19:02.351
Yeah?

19:02.658 --> 19:04.489
You okay?

19:05.194 --> 19:07.059
Been better.

19:08.297 --> 19:10.094
I'm coming in.

19:15.103 --> 19:16.331
Hi.

19:16.505 --> 19:17.938
Hi.

19:18.507 --> 19:20.099
Impressive.

19:21.076 --> 19:22.202
It's not me.

19:22.744 --> 19:24.439
No kidding.

19:24.613 --> 19:26.137
What is it?

19:40.762 --> 19:45.165
&lt;i>Oh. Burt Reynolds' Trans Am
from Smokey and the Bandit.&lt;/i>

19:46.835 --> 19:48.166
Yup.

19:50.005 --> 19:54.339
Would you care to explain why it's parked
in your handicapped spot?

19:55.210 --> 19:56.438
Not parked.

19:56.612 --> 19:57.874
Glued.

19:58.614 --> 20:01.447
- Ah. Rose?
- Rose.

20:01.617 --> 20:03.312
- Told you.
- You did.

20:03.485 --> 20:05.544
- But did you listen?
- Nope.

20:07.022 --> 20:08.887
Okay. Happy motoring.

20:37.719 --> 20:40.620
I feel bad it didn't work out
with Alan and Rose.

20:40.789 --> 20:43.622
Me too. Terrible.

20:44.493 --> 20:47.018
The problem is they jumped
into bed too fast.

20:47.629 --> 20:51.725
The problem is he doesn't keep
his glue solvent in his night stand.

20:52.834 --> 20:53.858
What's that mean?

20:55.170 --> 20:57.536
Another way of saying what you said.

20:59.041 --> 21:00.372
Ow.

21:08.083 --> 21:09.243
What's wrong with him?

21:10.986 --> 21:13.181
Little car accident.
